WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.959 --> 00:00:06.470
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and during my
episode 3 review I asked you all to submit

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:09.929
questions about the big WTF change to Jaime’s
character and all the other big moments.

00:00:09.929 --> 00:00:13.500
So I picked 10 of them to answer in this video
with one bonus questions.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.369
We’ve also got to give a high five to this
week’s giveaway winner Theresa Harris

00:00:16.369 --> 00:00:19.579
You win a $20 amazon gift card, I’ll be
‘DMing you on your channel for details.

00:00:19.579 --> 00:00:22.529
Next round starts when I post my episode 4
video.

00:00:22.529 --> 00:00:26.570
If you’re finding me for the first time
I’m just doing a weekly giveaway to say

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:28.979
thanks to all you guys for being so awesome.

00:00:28.979 --> 00:00:32.360
So we have a lot to talk about, since so many
people were so upset about what happened with

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:34.750
Jaime’s character I wanted to address that
first.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:39.790
So just because this was a pretty big deal
everybody please be nice to each other no

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:43.730
matter what your opinion is on the matter.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:47.460
Careful for spoilers from the episode if you
haven’t seen it yet but here we go.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.510
Question 1 - Bloody Desires asks Do you think
the way Jaime was durning that scene was out

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:55.820
of character considering his development so
far?

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:59.480
Considering he saved Brienne from getting
raped before they cut his hand off.

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:03.260
Yes definitely, George RR Martin even wrote
something on his blog about it.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:08.040
He basically said that because the show brought
Jaime back to King’s Landing earlier, the

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:10.600
whole dynamic between him and Cersei changed.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:15.250
In the book version of that scene, Cersei
is seeing Jaime for the first time and she

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.180
wants him as badly as he wants her.

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:18.180
Her only hesitancy is that they’ll be caught.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.130
But on the show because Jaime has been back
for weeks and they’ve been fighting the

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:22.000
whole context is changed.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:28.310
Martin also kind of distanced himself also
by saying that he never talked to D and D

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:29.700
about the scene.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:33.270
I think it’s unfortunate because Jaime’s
character is supposed to be on something of

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:34.270
a redemptive arc.

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:35.890
He’s trying to be more like Brienne.

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:37.720
And this scene destroyed that.

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:42.280
They have follow up scenes next week which
will spell out a little more where the show

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:43.940
is taking Jaime this season.

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:49.380
I think the other question we need to ponder
in the comments below is whether or not they

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:52.689
just made mistakes in the writing and filming
on the scene.

00:01:52.689 --> 00:01:56.210
Did they intend for it to be the way we saw
it or did the actors and the director just

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:57.960
go to far while they were filming it?

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:02.649
Question 2 - Valentino asks When do you think
Stannis will march on the wall?

00:02:02.649 --> 00:02:06.250
Not before Davos follows up on that letter
to the Iron Bank of Braavos.

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:09.619
Remember that scene where the boat passes
underneath it in the trailer?

00:02:09.619 --> 00:02:11.101
I think that was Daavos visiting the bank.

00:02:11.101 --> 00:02:15.630
The bank has really started to become a plot
point this season.

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:19.990
Remember how the crown is in debt to them
big time, Lady Olenna was talking to Tywin

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:23.610
about it and he kind of shrugged it off.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:28.360
It sounds like Daavos is going to use that
to get money from the Iron Bank.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:32.530
But I’m really interested to see if they
become a much bigger part of the story in

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:33.530
the future.

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:37.790
Promises to the bank have to be kept.

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:40.610
Otherwise they’ll turn around and fund your
enemies.

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:45.240
Question 3 - Steve Sunny asks why is Dorne
an Independent Kingdom

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:49.560
So I actually got a bunch of questions about
Dorne and why they have a Prince but not a

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:53.790
King and how they were able to resist Aegon
Targaryen’s Conquest of Westeros.

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:56.390
So this is meant to collectively sum up all
the answers.

00:02:56.390 --> 00:03:01.800
The reason Dorne has a prince but not a King
is that when Aegon Targaryen conquered Westeros

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:06.000
Dorne used much smarter military tactics and
because of the desert and the mountains they

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.760
were able to drive the Targaryen’s out.

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:13.350
Their covert tactics made it so that the Targaryen’s
couldn’t use their dragons like they did

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:15.690
on all the other armies.

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:21.320
Then by the time Baelor the Blessed became
king, remember Twyin mentioned him in his

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:26.280
speech to Tommen, he used a bunch of marriage
pacts to bring Dorne into the kingdom.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:31.230
But as part of that arrangement, each new
ruler of Dorne got to keep the title Prince.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:35.331
So there’s only one King of Westeros, but
Dorne still has a prince, whereas all the

00:03:35.331 --> 00:03:38.730
other noble houses are just Lords and Ladies.

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:44.300
Right now Myrcella is betrothed to one of
the really young Martell princes.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.580
Question 4 - Sairys Torres asks Who’s the
King now?

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:48.510
And is Margeary the Queen?

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:50.520
Tommen is the king if that wasn’t clear
in the episode.

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:55.430
But until he’s old enough to make political
and policy decisions, Tywin will effectively

00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:56.430
be the real ruler.

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:58.880
Tommen will just be a figurehead until then.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:01.540
In the books they make him sound much much
younger.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:04.220
The actor on the show almost looks like a
teenager.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:09.060
He was seven in season 1, so now he’s supposed
to be like 10 or 11 I think.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:11.290
So they aged him up.

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:16.010
In the book all they really let him do is
stamp documents as if it’s a game.

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:18.120
Like you would finger paint.

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:23.050
Except he’s finger painting the royal seal
on important documents.

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:26.530
Just another example of a big change the show
has made whether you agree with it or not.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:30.949
Question 5 - Danny Stones asks do you think
Littlefinger is going to train Sansa to play

00:04:30.949 --> 00:04:31.949
the Game of Thrones?

00:04:31.949 --> 00:04:34.690
I don’t think she’s going to follow the
same path as Arya, she’s not going to turn

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:36.449
into a super spy or anything.

00:04:36.449 --> 00:04:39.850
I hope that she gets wiser and more cunning.

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:44.460
Until now the most common adjective used to
describe her has been sweet as in Sweet Sansa.

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:50.110
She is kind of like a leaf being blown around
by all these big forces and up to now, she’s

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:54.990
kind of just done and believed whatever anyone
has told her.

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:58.050
So hopefully this season we’ll see her do
something really cool.

00:04:58.050 --> 00:05:04.139
If you’re reading the books, she’s going
to be a POV character in Winds of Winter.

00:05:04.139 --> 00:05:07.379
So I’m hoping for some badass Sansa moments.

00:05:07.379 --> 00:05:09.330
But don’t hold your breathe.

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:14.510
Question 6 - Peter Cho asks Why are the cannibals
traveling with Ygritte's group?

00:05:14.510 --> 00:05:18.990
The Thenns are just part of the raiding party
that’s trying to open that gate at Castle

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:19.990
Black.

00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:21.219
It can only be opened from the other side
of the wall.

00:05:21.219 --> 00:05:24.199
So Mance Rayder can’t bring his army through
until it’s opened.

00:05:24.199 --> 00:05:28.510
And the wildlings can’t open it until they
eat a lot of crow.

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:32.699
In the books the Thenns weren’t cannibals,
but another tribe of wildlings were.

00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:37.550
There are a ton of them, so the show had to
cut a bunch of them out of the story.

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:40.919
I think for one of my bonus videos in the
future I’ll do a wildling video and talk

00:05:40.919 --> 00:05:41.919
about each of the tribes.

00:05:41.919 --> 00:05:45.610
They’re really interesting, but there’s
so many of them you kind of have to do a separate

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:46.610
video for it.

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:50.810
Question 7 - Casey asks Do you think Tywin
is taking Tommen under his wing because he

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:53.500
doesn’t want another Joffrey situation?

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:57.460
I definitely think he’s aware Tommen is
open to suggestion.

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:00.000
Remember how he went straight to marriage
and heirs.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.509
He’s all about the Lannister bloodline and
duty to family.

00:06:03.509 --> 00:06:05.550
Mostly that the line continues.

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:09.199
Instead of the birds and the bees, with him
it’s more like the Business and the bees.

00:06:09.199 --> 00:06:13.840
I don’t think he’s necessarily evil, he’s
more like a grumpy Vulcan.

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:23.050
He has this vision for his family and the
kingdom and now, he thinks he’s in a place

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:26.009
where people won’t cause him so many problems.

00:06:26.009 --> 00:06:30.540
The big issue with Joffrey was that he made
decisions without consulting Tywin or he just

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:32.259
flat out did the opposite.

00:06:32.259 --> 00:06:36.599
The first really good example was beheading
Ned Stark.

00:06:36.599 --> 00:06:40.889
Tywin wouldn’t have done that, it’s primarily
what started the War of the Five Kings.

00:06:40.889 --> 00:06:46.539
Question 8 - Chad Morton (no avatar) asks
Why does Alliser Thorne hate Jon Snow?

00:06:46.539 --> 00:06:52.949
When Jon first came to the watch Alliser who
was the master at arms just mocked him by

00:06:52.949 --> 00:06:57.120
calling him Lord Snow, just making fun of
the fact he was a highborn Bastard who ended

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:58.509
up at the Night’s Watch.

00:06:58.509 --> 00:07:01.800
Which is kind of like the ultimate Chain Gang
of Westeros.

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:07.569
Eventually Jon made fun of him back and that’s
when Alliser started to outright hate him.

00:07:07.569 --> 00:07:09.249
Bullies don’t like to be bullied themselves.

00:07:09.249 --> 00:07:11.569
It’s not a very good reason to hate someone.

00:07:11.569 --> 00:07:14.809
But the book version of the character is a
very petty person.

00:07:14.809 --> 00:07:18.849
Question 9 - Gaz2D2 (no avatar) asks Do you
think the Game of Thrones TV show will feature

00:07:18.849 --> 00:07:24.059
any flashbacks?﻿

00:07:24.059 --> 00:07:27.800
I think there will be some flashbacks when
Bran finally meets the Three-Eyed Raven.

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:31.430
He’ll tell Bran his story, how he came to
be where his is.

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:34.309
So they’ll have to show something from his
past.

00:07:34.309 --> 00:07:37.970
It just seems too cool not to, especially
with that dream sequence they did when Bran

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:39.840
warged with the tree.

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:47.889
That bonus video I’m doing on Sunday is
for the Bloodraven, that was one of his names

00:07:47.889 --> 00:07:49.559
before he became the Three-Eyed Raven.

00:07:49.559 --> 00:07:52.120
So it will explain his history in Westeros
in much greater detail.

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:53.120
It’s pretty cool.

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:56.099
I won’t talk about anything that’s going
to happen in the future on the show though.

00:07:56.099 --> 00:08:00.129
Question 10 - Martin asks Do you feel that
the Hound has become more docile since teaming

00:08:00.129 --> 00:08:01.559
up with Arya?

00:08:01.559 --> 00:08:05.520
I think Arya is rubbing off on him and every
once and a while he acknowledges it, then

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:08.789
does everything he can to shake it off.

00:08:08.789 --> 00:08:10.629
Like when they were taken in by the farmer.

00:08:10.629 --> 00:08:14.199
He played along and you could see he thought
about staying and helping them.

00:08:14.199 --> 00:08:19.069
But then by morning his own sense of self-loathing
rises up and he shakes of all the niceness

00:08:19.069 --> 00:08:20.559
and robs the hell out of them.

00:08:20.559 --> 00:08:25.479
It’s almost like he hates himself so much
that anytime anyone shows him kindness he

00:08:25.479 --> 00:08:28.150
doesn’t believe it or he treats it with
disgust.

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:33.500
I really think Arya is getting tired of him.

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:36.370
They have a kind of temporary truce going
right now.

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:41.050
Arya knows he can help her get away and the
Hound knows she’s still worth money to someone.

00:08:41.050 --> 00:08:46.530
And one last Bonus Question - side effect
(no avatar) asks How big role will Mark Gatiss

00:08:46.530 --> 00:08:47.530
have?﻿

00:08:47.530 --> 00:08:50.520
I don’t think it will be Mycroft big if
that’s what you’re wondering.

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:52.710
He’s playing someone who works for the Iron
Bank.

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:55.060
I haven’t seen him on the show yet.

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:58.440
So I think when we see Braavos we’ll see
him.

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:04.390
Daavos is going to have to borrow a lot of
money to get Stannis an Army.

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:08.850
There was a shout out for the Gold Company,
so he might try to use the money to hire them

00:09:08.850 --> 00:09:10.590
as a mercenary army.

00:09:10.590 --> 00:09:15.451
Which reminds me, even if that doesn’t end
up happening, I’ll do a bonus video for

00:09:15.451 --> 00:09:16.620
some of the mercenary companies eventually.

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:18.080
One for the Second Sons and one for the Gold
Company.

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:21.070
They both have a really cool history.

00:09:21.070 --> 00:09:26.591
So thank you so much for submitting questions,
I’m sure the Jaime Cersei debate will go

00:09:26.591 --> 00:09:32.520
on forever, but like I said my next bonus
video will be the Bloodraven on Sunday.

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:33.661
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:09:33.661 --> 00:09:37.530
And leave me suggestions for other bonus videos
to do in the comments.

